Use the frontend-design skill to fix the Kairos Client Workspace architecture, client navigation and performance.

The existing Client Workspace is functional but has three major usability problems. I want actual implementation changes, not another high-level design proposal.

## Problem 1: Workspace tabs are not real tabs

The current Overview, Opportunity, Options, Simulator, Portfolio and Notes tabs navigate vertically through sections of one long page.

This is unacceptable.

Replace the current anchor-scroll navigation with real, independently displayed workspace panels.

Requirements:
- A persistent client header and tab bar.
- Only the active workspace is visible.
- Tab selection changes the main content area, not the page's scroll position.
- Each tab uses the existing corresponding components and functionality.
- Switching tabs should feel like switching workspaces in a professional desktop application.
- Provide subtle transitions, approximately 150–220ms.
- Maintain scroll position independently per workspace when practical.
- Preserve simulator inputs, selected products and advisor notes between tabs.
- Do not recreate the underlying components.
- Deep links must open the correct client and active workspace.
- Existing legacy URLs containing fragments such as #options must remain compatible.
- Browser back and forward navigation must work.

Do not render all six heavy views unnecessarily. Preserve important state in a shared client-specific state layer rather than relying entirely on mounted component state.

## Problem 2: Client rail cannot collapse or filter properly

The left client rail takes too much room and is difficult to navigate.

Implement:
- An explicit collapse/expand button.
- Expanded width approximately 240px.
- Collapsed width approximately 56–64px.
- Search clients by name.
- Filters for opportunity type and review status, using existing data.
- Clear active-filter indicators and reset filters.
- Smooth client switching.
- Selected client visible in either mode.
- In collapsed mode, show avatars or initials and accessible tooltips.
- Animate the main workspace expanding into reclaimed space.
- Preserve sidebar state across tab changes.
- Never reset the selected client or simulator just because the rail collapses.
- Preserve the existing homepage client-card shared-layout animation.

Place search and filters in the rail itself, not on another page.

## Problem 3: Client workspace is too slow

Before optimizing, profile the actual behaviour.

Inspect:
- Network requests and asset sizes.
- React re-rendering and mount behaviour.
- Heavy 3D scene imports.
- Portfolio simulator calculations.
- Client state updates.
- Animation-related layout work.
- Duplicate or unnecessary data transformation.
- Development-mode overhead versus production performance.

Record a baseline for initial client opening and tab switching.

Implement targeted optimizations such as:
- Route-level/component-level code splitting.
- Lazy loading the simulator and 3D journey.
- Prefetching likely next workspaces when useful.
- Memoization only where profiling supports it.
- Preserving heavy component state outside the rendering lifecycle.
- Avoiding unnecessary WebGL mounting when the 3D journey is not active.

Do not install optimization libraries without justification.

